# Preliminary Sentiment Analysis Report

## 1. Objective

This report presents the preliminary sentiment analysis and product issue classification conducted as part of the Sciencia AI sentiment analytics project.

The objective is to explore how user reviews can be transformed into structured insights that help identify customer sentiment and product-related pain points.

## 2. Dataset Overview

The analysis used 489 reviews retained as English-language reviews after preliminary language identification and filtering.

The dataset covered three applications:

- Notion
- Duolingo
- Spotify

| Application | Reviews Analyzed |
|---|---:|
| Notion | 175 |
| Duolingo | 161 |
| Spotify | 153 |
| **Total** | **489** |

## 3. Sentiment Analysis Method

VADER (Valence Aware Dictionary and sEntiment Reasoner) was used to estimate the sentiment polarity of each review.

The compound score was used to assign sentiment labels:

| Compound Score | Sentiment |
|---|---|
| Greater than or equal to 0.05 | Positive |
| Less than or equal to -0.05 | Negative |
| Between -0.05 and 0.05 | Neutral |

A small number of predictions were manually reviewed and corrected when the original classification appeared inconsistent with the review's expressed meaning.

Manual corrections were recorded separately from the original VADER predictions.

## 4. Overall Sentiment Distribution

| Sentiment | Number of Reviews | Percentage |
|---|---:|---:|
| Positive | 346 | 70.8% |
